# Frontend rules (Inertia 2 + Vue 3)

## Project structure

- Entry point: `resources/js/app.ts`.
- Page components (Inertia pages): `resources/js/pages/` — match the route name.
- Reusable components: `resources/js/components/`.
- shadcn-vue / reka-ui primitives: `resources/js/components/ui/<kind>/`. Don't
  hand-write new primitives — extend the existing ones.
- Layouts: `resources/js/layouts/{app,auth,settings}/`.
- Composables: `resources/js/composables/`.
- Helpers / utils: `resources/js/lib/utils.ts`.
- TypeScript types: `resources/js/types/`.

## Vue / TypeScript

- Use `<script setup lang="ts">` for new components — never the Options API.
- Type props explicitly (`defineProps<{ ... }>()`); don't rely on inference for public APIs.
- Provide defaults via `withDefaults()` so the component renders without required props.
- Use `defineEmits<{ (e: 'name', payload: T): void }>()` for typed events.
- Prefer composables (`useX`) over mixins. There's `composables/useAppearance.ts`,
  `useInitials.ts` — match that pattern.
- Imports use the `@/` alias (configured in `vite.config.ts`) for `resources/js/*`.

## Tailwind

- Tailwind 4 — utilities-first; no `@apply` for trivial styling.
- Use `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` for conditional class names — never string concat.
- Stick to existing design tokens (defined in `resources/css/app.css`). If you need
  a new color/spacing, add it to the Tailwind config / CSS variables, not inline.
- Mobile-first responsive: default styles are mobile, scale up with `md:`, `lg:`.

## Inertia

- Page components must default-export.
- Use `usePage()` for shared props passed from `HandleInertiaRequests` middleware.
- Form helpers: `useForm()` from `@inertiajs/vue3` for submissions — don't roll your own.
- Navigation: `<Link>` component or `router.visit()`, never `<a href>` for in-app routes.
- CSRF 419 errors are handled centrally in `bootstrap/app.php` via a full location visit.
  Don't try to handle them in components.

## Forms / inputs

- Use the `Input`, `Label`, `Button`, `Checkbox` components from `components/ui/`.
- Validation errors come from `useForm().errors`. Display next to the field.
- Submit on `@submit.prevent` with `form.post(route('...'))`.

## Icons

- Use `lucide-vue-next` (already installed). Import only what you use:
  `import { Camera, User } from 'lucide-vue-next'`.
- Don't pull in Font Awesome or Heroicons — keeps bundle small.

## Don't

- Don't reach into Filament from the Vue side; they're separate apps on the same domain.
- Don't add new dependencies without checking they're not already in `package.json`.
- Don't bypass `vite.config.ts` aliases — fix the alias instead.
